Z||000000||speed racer||12-11-2001||10:35 PM||||My seats are all wore out and broken down I was wondering what bucket seats would fit in my car. If they don’t fit on the track could I just drill new holes?<BR>Kyle<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||12-11-2001||11:34 PM||||I hate to say it but, this is a good one for the 'search' function.  There are quite a number of threads on this and lots of seats that will fit.  Many will need a little modification if you want to use the stock Fiero seat rails. Go forth with your measuring tape and have fun.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signat.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000002||speed racer||12-11-2001||11:53 PM||||I used the search, but I didn’t find what I need I want some good buckets that fit like a glove and I don’t what the shoulders to stick out form the console I want the bottom to fit like the backseat of a 94 Camaro but still be able to get in and out easily.<BR>I did read that the 2nd gen mr2 seats were comfortable. Has any one ever tried that.<BR>Kyle<BR><p>[This message has been edited by speed racer (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
