Z||000007||deceler8||12-12-2001||11:03 AM||||Grand Am, Cavalier, Sunbird seats will all fit, but you'll have to use the Fiero tracks.<P>No problem...the seat tracks bolt right on. <P>There's lots more of the above seats in the yards than Camaro or Firebird seats and they'll be cheaper.||||reg||1
Z||000008||RacinRob||12-12-2001||11:26 AM||||Right now I'm driving a 91 Cav. and my two cents are (is) they suck!||||reg||1
Z||000009||honegod||12-12-2001||07:53 PM||||I tried a grand am seat in my 84, the tracks bolted right up, but the seat bottom foam was about 3" thicker than the fieros, it felt like sitting on a phone book, way too tall. I'm 5'11" so shorter folks might like it, I didn't.<BR>presumably the firebird seat bottoms are suitably thin.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cooter||12-12-2001||08:37 PM||||I have the mid 90's Trans-Am seats with lumbar and they are pretty nice. Because of the seat design, you can not use the Fiero seat track on the driver's seat- the bolt holes are in different places on the seat bottom, but with a little grindage, the Trans-Am seat track will fit the Fiero floor studs. You lose some head room because the seat sits higher on the T/A tracks, but I am 5'7" so the lost head room is not an issue.<BR>BTW- You can buy my dark grey leather seats if you want them- I will even let the passenger seat go with the Fiero track still on it, so it will be a direct bolt in.||||reg||1
Z||000011||speed racer||12-12-2001||09:09 PM||||I don't really want to be any higher I like the top of the doors coming up to my shoulders.<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
